  // ─── [/DRAFT-LAYOUT] ──────────────────────────────────────────────

  // ─── [DRAFT-CHECK] ────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Reads the assembled draft and finds what is WRONG WITH IT AS A DOCUMENT,
  // deterministically, before any model is asked its opinion.
  //
  // These are the mistakes drafting-by-section actually makes, and every one
  // of them is machine-checkable — so checking them with an AI would be both
  // slower and less reliable:
  //   - a capitalised term used everywhere and never defined
  //   - a definition written once and never used
  //   - "as set out in Section 12" in a nine-section agreement
  //   - the counterparty called three different things
  //   - a [[Placeholder]] left in what looks like a final draft
  //   - two sections with the same name, or a gap in the numbering
  //
  // Severity is "blocker" for things that make the document wrong, "warn"
  // for things a human should look at. Nothing here edits anything.
  // TO REMOVE: delete to [/DRAFT-CHECK] + _runDraftCheck's callers.

  // Words that are capitalised for reasons other than being defined terms.
  var DC_NOT_TERMS = ("The A An And Or Of To In For By With If Each Either Both This That These Those " +
